WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.020
Five adult specimens of SCP-939 were selected
for testing with The Clockworks.

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:09.430
“Rough” produced an output of a pile of
bone splinters, broken teeth, and pieces of

00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:11.230
translucent red tissue.

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:15.379
This tissue continued to move and twitch on
an occasional basis for several hours before

00:00:15.379 --> 00:00:16.379
stopping.

00:00:16.379 --> 00:00:20.070
The specimen run through the machine on “Coarse,”
produced several neat, organized piles of

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:25.849
tissue, including its muscles, ground-up bones,
teeth, skin, esophagus, and fifteen kilograms

00:00:25.849 --> 00:00:29.539
of rotten human flesh with a D-Class ID tag
on top.

00:00:29.539 --> 00:00:33.710
When the next specimen was input on “1:1,”
the output was [REDACTED]

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:37.200
The next specimen was placed on the setting
“Fine,” and it produced the exact same

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:40.120
specimen of adult SCP-939.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:43.210
The only notable difference was that it had
stopped breathing.

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:47.860
On the setting “Very Fine,” the experiment
produced a pile of smoldering white ash.

